//? Title: SegNet pooling indices and sparse decoding
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Recovering pixel labels from pooled CNN features requires restoring lost spatial detail. SegNet reuses encoder maximum locations for sparse decoder unpooling; this report checks exact values/derivatives before a visible tensor Adam fit and held-out mask evaluation.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/segnet.cpp`.

> The method

The encoder saves detached2x2 maximum indices. Sparse unpooling restores values to those positions and convolution densifies the result. Full and compact VGG-style graphs preserve original odd shapes,and learned/BN state are checkpointed together during explicit optimization.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/segnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/segnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/segnet_concept.tikz > build/segnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/segnet_concept.svg build/segnet_concept.dvi > build/segnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
