> Tensor winner indices and sparse unpooling

Each nonoverlapping2x2 encoder pool saves the first row-major maximum index.
The flattened NHWC index includes batch and channel offsets. Ordinary tensor
max-pooling supplies the differentiable values; the detached winner indices
are computed by tensor reshape/transpose/argmax and integer index arithmetic.
No host pixel-value scan or inverse-map arithmetic remains.

Unpool uses tensor segment scattering to restore values only at the saved
winners,with zeros everywhere else. This includes negative pooled values;
unpooling is not nearest interpolation. Saved pre-pool shapes restore odd
trailing rows/columns as zeros. Only values receive gradients through the
scatter. The independent native oracle checks every sparse value and derivative
for negative inputs,multiple batches/channels and odd5x7 shapes. Ties select
top-left first; malformed duplicate/out-of-range winner records are rejected.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/segnet_pooling.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  auto x = (n::arange(0, 35, 1, n::DType::Float64) * .1 - 4.)
               .reshape({1, 5, 7, 1})
               .requires_grad_();
  const auto record = m::SegNetPoolWithIndices(x);
  const auto restored = m::SegNetIndexUnpool(record.values, record),
             g = n::grad(n::sum(restored), {x})[0];
  const std::vector<std::int64_t> expected = {8, 10, 12, 22, 24, 26};
  if (record.indices.to_vector<std::int64_t>() != expected ||
      n::count_nonzero(g).item<int>() != 6)
    return 1;
  for (int row = 0; row < 5; ++row)
    for (int col = 0; col < 7; ++col) {
      const auto index = row * 7 + col;
      const bool winner = std::find(expected.begin(), expected.end(), index) != expected.end();
      if (std::abs(restored.at({0, row, col, 0}) - (winner ? x.at({0, row, col, 0}) : 0.)) >
              1e-12 ||
          g.at({0, row, col, 0}) != (winner ? 1 : 0))
        return 1;
    }
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(x.detach().reshape({5, 7}), {0}), -4, 0),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(restored.reshape({5, 7}), {0}), -4, 0),
       c = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(record.values.reshape({2, 3}), {0}), -4, 0),
       d = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(g.reshape({5, 7}), {0}), 0, 1);
  a.title("Negative5 by7 encoder input");
  b.title("Sparse unpool: zeros elsewhere");
  c.title("Six pooled maxima");
  d.title("Exact winner gradient footprint");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 2)
      .add(a)
      .add(b)
      .add(c)
      .add(d)
      .size(1200, 1000)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/segnet_pooling.svg");
  std::print("All35 sparse values and input derivatives exact;winner indices8/10/12/22/24/26. "
             "Odd row4 and column6 remain zero;negative winners are retained.\n");
}
```
