> Full and compact SegNet graphs and index-cache accounting

Thirteen VGG encoder convolutions and a mirrored decoder use BN/ReLU except
the final biased3x3 class predictor. Decoder stages unpool from saved encoder
indices,then convolve sparse features to form dense representations. No
pretrained weights or learned upsampling filters are used. BN has
momentum.9/epsilon1e-5 and eagerly updates moving moments during training.

The full RGB/11-class model has29,449,355 learned and15,872 moving-state
scalars,with all102 learned tensor gradients executed below at64x64.
The compact RGB/four-class model divides widths by8 and retains all stages.
Native tests require every compact derivative to be finite and nonzero and
check96/97-pixel alignment.

For even spatial sizes,an Int64 winner cache takes half the bytes of the
corresponding full Float32 pre-pool feature cache: one8-byte index replaces
four4-byte feature values. This compares index storage alone; returned pooled
values and autograd graphs also consume memory,so it is not a measured peak
training-memory reduction.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  {
    n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
    const auto net = n::models::SegNet(
        p, state, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 64 * 64 * 3)).reshape({1, 64, 64, 3}), {}, true);
    const auto g = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.logits)), p.parameters());
    if (p.count() != 29449355 || state.count() != 15872 || g.size() != 102)
      return 1;
    for (const auto &v : g)
      if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()))
        return 1;
    std::print(
        "Full SegNet:{} learned/{} state scalars,all{} finite defined gradients at64px.\n",
        p.count(), state.count(), g.size());
  }
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
  n::models::SegNetConfig c;
  c.classes = 4;
  c.width_divisor = 8;
  for (int side : {96, 97}) {
    const auto net = n::models::SegNet(p, state, n::zeros({2, side, side, 3}), c);
    if (net.logits.shape() != n::Shape{2, side, side, 4})
      return 1;
    std::int64_t index_bytes = 0, feature_bytes = 0;
    for (const auto &record : net.pooling) {
      index_bytes += 8 * record.indices.numel();
      feature_bytes += 4 * n::shape_numel(record.shape);
    }
    if (side == 96 && index_bytes * 2 != feature_bytes)
      return 1;
    std::print("Compact{}px:{} learned/{} state scalars;indices{} bytes versus original "
               "Float32 feature cache{} bytes,excluding pooled tensors/graphs.\n",
               side, p.count(), state.count(), index_bytes, feature_bytes);
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full SegNet:29449355 learned/15872 state scalars,all102 finite defined gradients at64px.
Compact96px:463132 learned/1984 state scalars;indices562176 bytes versus original Float32 feature cache1124352 bytes,excluding pooled tensors/graphs.
Compact97px:463132 learned/1984 state scalars;indices562176 bytes versus original Float32 feature cache1136704 bytes,excluding pooled tensors/graphs.
// result_end

> Actual procedural fitting images and masks

The tensor generator produces64 fitting/16 validation/16 test96-pixel RGB
shape scenes,seeds11/22/33. Brightness,noise and image-wide tint are independent
of shape class. Later objects occlude earlier labels. The tensor RNG changes
fixed-seed pixels from the legacy mt19937 implementation; this is an explicit
procedural adaptation. Palette: background dark,circle red,rectangle green,
triangle blue.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/segnet_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto data = m::TensorSegmentationShapes(64, 96, 11);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> gallery;
  const auto colored = m::ColorSegmentationLabels(n::slice_axis(data.labels, 0, 0, 4));
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    gallery.push_back(n::slice_axis(data.images, 0, i, i + 1));
    gallery.push_back(n::slice_axis(colored, 0, i, i + 1));
  }
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(gallery, 0), "build/segnet_data.png", 2, 0., 1., 3, 1., 2);
  const auto weights = m::SegmentationClassWeights(data.labels, 4);
  std::print(
      "64 fitting RGB images96x96; classes0 background,1 circle,2 rectangle,3 triangle. "
      "Fit-only inverse-square-root pseudocount weights {:.6f}/{:.6f}/{:.6f}/{:.6f}. "
      "Noise,tint and brightness are class-independent; later objects occlude earlier masks. "
      "Tensor RNG changes fixed-seed pixels relative to the old mt19937 generator.\n",
      weights.at({0}), weights.at({1}), weights.at({2}), weights.at({3}));
}
```
